>> servings: 24
>> tags: Baking, Biscuits

Preheat the oven to 160°C fan-forced. Line two trays with baking paper.

Mix the oats, flour, coconut and sugar in a large bowl. @rolled oats{1%cup} @plain flour{1%cup} @desiccated coconut{1%cup} @brown sugar{150%g}

Melt the @butter{125%g} and @golden syrup{2%tbsp} in a small saucepan over low heat.

Dissolve the bicarb in the @boiling water{2%tbsp}, stir into the @butter{125%g} mixture, then pour over the dry ingredients and mix well. @bicarbonate of soda{1%tsp}

Roll tablespoons of mixture into balls, place 5 cm apart and flatten slightly.

Bake ~{12%minutes} until golden. Cool on the trays for ~{5%minutes} before moving to a rack.
